# legacy / testdata
#
# testdata/ holds real customer project files and is never committed. The one
# exception is the Go fuzzing corpus: `go test -fuzz` writes a reproducer to
# testdata/fuzz/<Target>/ when it finds a crash, and that reproducer is the
# regression test. Without this exception a crash found by fuzzing could never
# be committed.
# Note the trailing /* rather than a bare testdata/: git cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory is itself excluded, so an exception under a
# `testdata/` rule would silently never match.
testdata/*
!testdata/fuzz/

# Exception: the two Twofish fixtures are ours, not customer data. They were
# generated with the ComponentAce DB Manager and hold a synthetic Employees
# table (three invented rows), so they carry no customer content and no vendor
# material -- only the format's own ABS0LUTEDATABASE/ABSP magic. They are
# committed because they are the only fixtures CI can use: without them every
# fixture-backed test skips on a runner and the crypto is never exercised.
# Keep this list explicit; never widen it to a glob that could catch a real
# customer file.
!testdata/Employees-Twofish_128.abs
!testdata/Employees-Twofish_256.abs
!testdata/README.md

legacy/